slide('Score the change and the preserved flights separately','<div class="check-row"><span>Requested segment range</span><b>Correct replacement</b></div><div class="check-row"><span>Untouched segments</span><b>Still present</b></div><div class="check-row"><span>Passenger approval</span><b>Before the write</b></div><div class="check-row"><span>Airline policy</span><b>Applicable rules met</b></div>','The state scorer is deterministic over recorded state. It does not use the agent’s final assertion as proof. A completion score must fail when the requested change is missing, even if the unchanged return is preserved.',211,'state-scoring')
slide('The explanation judge answers a different question','<div class="two-col"><div><h2>Booking-state check</h2><p>Was the approved itinerary applied without changing unrelated flights?</p></div><div><h2>Explanation judgment</h2><p>Did the final response accurately describe the recorded work and unresolved issues?</p></div></div><div class="callout">“Your return flight is unchanged” can be wrong even when it is polite and well formatted.</div>','The explanation judge receives the recorded work needed for its rubric. Human review and deterministic state checks remain distinct evidence. Missing judgments stay unavailable; do not average them as zero or success.',216,'separate-judge')
exercise('Add the booking check the old evaluation missed','Curate regression cases','my_state_scorer and my_judge_validation',['Implement preservation and confirmation checks; inspect the independent task-success score beside them.','Try the correct booking, missing return, and unconfirmed-write fixtures.','Keep the explanation judgment separate from those state checks.'],'Check my booking scorer → Check my judge-response validator → Save my development evaluation code','Your scorer rejects the missing return and an unapproved write.',221,'state-check','answer-state')
slide('Save the case and its checks with the checkpoint',flow([('Regression case','Original booking and reviewed expectation'),('Source files','Case builder and evaluation code'),('Checkpoint artifact','A saved version you can restore')])+'<p>A W&B Artifact is a versioned bundle of files. Open the checkpoint artifact and find the case inputs and source used for this exercise.</p><p class="caption">Saving locally and publishing the artifact are separate. If publication fails, retry the upload without rerunning the passenger request.</p>','Show the checkpoint link produced by the participant’s session. Ask someone to identify the source case, reviewer, and actual function. A named dataset without its initial booking cannot reproduce this incident.',228,'regression-artifact')
slide('Break until 4:00','<p class="sub">Save the regression dataset and selected criteria. We will test a code repair against them after the break.</p>','Ten-minute break. Do not edit final cases or resample cases based on which version looks better.',230,'break-two')
slide('Repair the list operation, then compare the behavior',itinerary([('Current list',ORIGINAL),('Repaired result',REPLACED)]),'Revisit the same concrete request. The implementation change builds a complete replacement itinerary from the requested range and untouched prefix and suffix. It does not depend on a flight-count heuristic.',240,'repair-problem')
slide('Replace a range without dropping its neighbors',code('def my_itinerary_builder(\n    current_flights, replace_start, replace_stop, replacement_flights\n):\n    return (\n        current_flights[:replace_start]\n        + replacement_flights\n        + current_flights[replace_stop:]\n    )','1-4|5|6|7|all')+'<p class="caption">Python uses a half-open range: the start is included; the stop is not. Validate the requested range before use.</p>','The example replaces original[0:2] with one flight and preserves original[2:]. Do not assume every request changes one flight. A full-itinerary change legitimately has start zero and stop len(original).',246,'range-repair')
slide('Walk through the values before running the model',code('original = ["outbound-1", "outbound-2", "return-1"]\nstart, stop = 0, 2\nreplacement = ["new-outbound"]\n\noriginal[:start]   # []\nreplacement       # ["new-outbound"]\noriginal[stop:]    # ["return-1"]','1-3|5|6|7|all')+'<p>The complete API input becomes <code>["new-outbound", "return-1"]</code>.</p>','This is a free, simplified arithmetic check. It establishes the list transformation, not whether the model selected the correct segment range or received passenger confirmation.',250,'range-values')
exercise('Test the repair on matched development bookings','Repair itinerary handling','my_itinerary_builder',['Implement the range replacement and validate its bounds.','Test a one-way case, connecting itinerary, and full replacement.','Run the curated regression cases, then compare both versions on the development bookings.'],'Check my itinerary repair → Run my curated regression cases → Compare on four development bookings','Each pair starts from the same state and records the exact builder that ran.',255,'repair','answer-builder')
slide('The passenger must approve the proposed change',flow([('Agent proposes','Full resulting itinerary'),('Scripted passenger checks','Request and preserved flights'),('Confirmation','Only when requirements match'),('Write','Apply the approved change')])+'<p>The passenger script must reject an unrelated change. It cannot blindly approve every proposal to make the exercise complete.</p>','Confirm that the scripted passenger enforces the source request’s requirements. A correct refusal or request for clarification may be the right outcome. The code repair cannot compensate for an incorrect approval policy.',264,'confirmation')
slide('Explain a passing repair without overstating it','<div class="comparison-grid"><div><h2>Local fixture</h2><p>The repaired function preserves the return in the known list-replacement example.</p></div><div><h2>Agent behavior</h2><p>The agent still has to select the right flights, ask for approval, and report the result.</p></div></div><p>The worked repair establishes a mechanism. The matched evaluations establish how the tested agent behaved.</p>','Keep deterministic repair results separate from live stochastic outcomes. A live success remains a success. Never replace it with a failure to improve the story.',272,'repair-boundary')
exercise('Judge one saved explanation against its evidence','Build regression cases','my_judge_validation and the explanation rubric',['Choose a saved development execution.','Read the booking result and the final response together.','Run one explicit judgment and inspect its cited event IDs.'],'Judge this saved explanation','The response validates, and its cited events support or contradict its reason.',273,'judge-execution','answer-judge')
slide('Freeze code before opening the reserved requests',flow([('Development results','Read successes and failures'),('Select the tested repair','Save the exact source'),('Freeze versions','Keep original and repair'),('Reserved evaluation','No more choosing on these cases')])+'<p>If the repair regresses, retain the earlier version and explain why. A longer instruction or extra check does not earn a release.</p>','Final expected answers do not enter the solver or rubric-tuning contexts. The local source files are inspectable for teaching, so this is a controlled workshop comparison, not a secure blind benchmark.',280,'freeze')
exercise('Compare six reserved bookings across both versions','Evaluate the frozen versions','The matched evaluation call',['Freeze the tested repair and inspect its source reference.','Run both versions on the six fixed reserved requests.','Open one aligned case and follow both rows back to their traces.'],'Freeze the tested repair → Evaluate six reserved bookings','All twelve executions have matched case identities, or an explicit unavailable status.',286,'final')
slide('Read the same request across the two versions',table(['Same case','Starting version','Repaired version'],[['Initial state','Same reservation snapshot','Same reservation snapshot'],['Executed code','Starting builder source','Frozen repair source'],['Booking outcome','Read actual final flights','Read actual final flights'],['Explanation','Inspect its own judge result','Inspect its own judge result'],['Operational measures','Time, errors, usage','Time, errors, usage']]),'Teach the alignment before opening EvalTables. Compare the complete booking state; do not substitute a tag result for deterministic correctness. Match source IDs and execution fingerprints.',294,'aligned-comparison')
capture('evaltables','Follow an aligned case back to its booking','Recorded native EvalTables comparison.',299,'Choose an identical case in the two versions. Read the state scores, output booking, judgment status, and trace links.')
capture('evaltables-case','Read both outputs for the same request','Recorded aligned development case.',302,'Identify the shared input and the separate predictions. Open the underlying booking and native trace before explaining a passing score.')
slide('The recorded agent comparison was a tie',table(['Reserved requests','Starting agent','Agent with itinerary builder'],[['Final evaluation','6 / 6 task checks passed','6 / 6 task checks passed'],['Subsequent traffic','4 / 4 task checks passed','4 / 4 task checks passed']])+'<p>All 40 qualification conversations passed their task checks. The live agent did not reproduce the missing-return defect.</p><p class="caption">The labeled local adapter drill demonstrates the repair mechanism separately. Native Alignment judging was unavailable, so this result says nothing about monitor accuracy.</p>','Preserve the successful baseline. Do not describe the helper as improving task quality on this rehearsal. The controlled drill is a real code repair, but it is not a spontaneous agent failure. These small simulated batches do not estimate production reliability.',305,'recorded-results',source='https://github.com/ash0ts/forge-workshop-kit/blob/main/examples/airline-monitoring/qualification.json')
slide('Report denominators and unresolved work',table(['Measure','Report together'],[['Requested changes completed','Passed cases / scored cases; unavailable cases'],['Unrequested changes','Count and the affected segment'],['Monitoring accuracy','Reviewed precision, recall, and coverage'],['Explanation quality','Judged rows and missing judgments'],['Operational cost','Known cost, bounded unknown usage, native tag cost status']]),'A six-case comparison has limited reach. Show each failure and avoid a general claim that monitoring improves all agents. If all cases tie, inspect whether behavior or cost changed while correctness stayed equal.',308,'report-measures')
slide('Use later traffic to check the frozen monitor',flow([('Four new requests','Reserved from development'),('Two isolated versions','Same original booking per pair'),('Same saved tag','Frozen criteria'),('Read judgments','Coverage and disagreements')])+'<p>This is a bounded subsequent traffic batch. It is not a production rollout or proof of performance under changing real traffic.</p>','The subsequent batch is separate from the six final requests. Do not tune the monitor after seeing one version’s outcomes. Read the differences between state outcomes and tag classifications.',320,'subsequent')
exercise('Check what the monitor catches after the repair','Monitor subsequent requests','my_monitor',['Run both versions on the subsequent batch.','Read tag results after native processing completes.','Inspect at least one tagged and one untagged request.'],"Monitor four subsequent requests → Read the subsequent batch's tag results",'You can distinguish fewer booking failures from fewer judgments being available.',326,'traffic')
slide('A falling alert count has several explanations','<div class="bundle-list"><div>Fewer task failures<small>Confirm with reviewed booking states</small></div><div>Lower processing coverage<small>Check pending and failed tag judgments</small></div><div>A changed request mix<small>Compare the batch and reservation families</small></div><div>A changed rule<small>Compare the saved criteria snapshot</small></div></div>','Ask participants to rule out each explanation with the records. A workshop that simply celebrates a downward chart has skipped the measurement problem it was meant to teach.',337,'alerts')
slide('Write down what changed and whether it helped','<div class="timeline-list"><b>Agent</b><span>Which booking outcomes changed on matched requests?</span><b>Monitor</b><span>Which failures did the reviewed rule find or miss?</span><b>Evaluation</b><span>Which new check would catch this problem before release?</span><b>Next test</b><span>What remains uncertain, and which request would test it?</span></div>','The participant conclusion should cite one actual case and its exact code, booking, trace, and evaluation. Improvements are welcome; a documented tie or regression also completes the lesson.',345,'conclusion')
exercise('Publish the comparison and stop automatic judging','Write the conclusion','The saved report and tag readback',['Publish saved comparisons; retry missing exports without rerunning requests.','Write the conclusion with one supporting case and one remaining failure.','Disable the workshop tag, then verify its native state.'],'Publish saved comparisons → Publish my conclusion → Verify automatic tagging is off','The Report opens its supporting evidence, and automatic judging is confirmed off.',350,'report')
slide('The next release has a check the first release lacked','<p class="principle">You can point to a passenger request, the booking change, the monitoring decision, and the regression check that tests it again.</p><p>The final comparison tells you whether this repair is worth keeping. The next incident may need a different rule.</p>','End by asking someone to reproduce a case from its saved initial state. Do not conclude with a promise of autonomous improvement. Monitoring, human review, and offline evaluation each answered a different question.',358,'end')

